      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T08:09:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem to work if user uses WaitAny to wait for the map async callback when the buffer is not used by the GPU.\n\nFor example:\n```\n// assuming buffer is not used by the GPU\nauto future \u003d buffer.MapAsync([]{});\n\n// Since there is no GPU usage of this buffer, the front-end might return\n// immediately without flushing any GL command\ninstance.WaitAny(future, UINT64_MAX);\n\n// This will return nullptr\nvoid* mappedPtr \u003d buffer.GetMappedRange();\n```\n\nIf we want `WantAny` to wait for the enqueued GL `MapBufferRange` command to run, we might need to call `TrackUsage` here.\n```suggestion\n    TrackUsage();\n\n    return ToBackend(GetDevice())\n        -\u003eEnqueueGL([this, self \u003d Ref\u003cBuffer\u003e(this), offset, size,\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "a9f5b656016c26330e1b0d38581a3f2abd6a3935",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef293e43_b4eeea28",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/BufferGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 237,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000024
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T17:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\nI don\u0027t have a good sense of the cost here. Should we do this only for deferral?",
      "parentUuid": "b6d6d15a_86560e73",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "a9f5b656016c26330e1b0d38581a3f2abd6a3935",
