      "writtenOn": "2026-02-12T08:29:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think we should only do that for `GLDefer`. So that we can avoid the latency for non-deferred path.",
      "parentUuid": "ef293e43_b4eeea28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 236,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "a9f5b656016c26330e1b0d38581a3f2abd6a3935",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aaa3727a_325c43a1",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/BufferGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T08:09:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be quite confusing for readers to understand why we have to use DestroyGL here.\n\nAn alternative way is just early return if newState \u003d\u003d Destroyed.\nThe buffer will be implicitly unmapped when it\u0027s destroyed by `glDeleteBuffers` anw.\nAccording to the GL ES 3.0 spec\u0027s `2.10.3.1 Unmapping Buffers` section:\n\u003e Buffers are implicitly unmapped as a side effect of deletion or reinitialization\n(i.e. calling DeleteBuffers or BufferData).\n\n```suggestion\n    if (newState \u003d\u003d Destroyed) {\n    \treturn;\n    }\n    IgnoreErrors(device-\u003eEnqueueGL([this]() { UnmapBuffer(...) }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "a9f5b656016c26330e1b0d38581a3f2abd6a3935",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a9ac411_ff0e4526",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/BufferGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000024
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T17:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good idea. Done.\n\nNote that, combined with the MappedAtCreation change, this will skip the mapping and memcpy\u0027ing of the CPU staging buffer for mappedAtCreation buffers as well. \nThis seems ok, and in fact, better than attempting to defer it, since we\u0027d \nlikely have to make a copy that outlasts the Buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "aaa3727a_325c43a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 276,
